WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.710 --> 00:00:01.543
- [Mark] All right, Johnny.

00:00:01.543 --> 00:00:03.507
Johnny, what neighborhood
did you grow up in?

00:00:03.507 --> 00:00:05.698
- I'm from Santa Fe Springs, Canta Ranas,

00:00:05.698 --> 00:00:08.466
that's Southeast L.A.
and Whittier and Norwalk.

00:00:08.466 --> 00:00:10.780
We're the only neighborhood in two cities.

00:00:10.780 --> 00:00:12.660
We take up a section of Whittier

00:00:12.660 --> 00:00:14.322
and Santa Fe Springs,

00:00:14.322 --> 00:00:17.470
so we're the only gang in Southeast L.A.

00:00:17.470 --> 00:00:19.340
That occupies two cities.

00:00:19.340 --> 00:00:20.590
- [Mark] So it has to be a big gang?

00:00:20.590 --> 00:00:21.580
- Yeah, we're a big gang.

00:00:21.580 --> 00:00:23.746
We came out in 1941, but we used

00:00:23.746 --> 00:00:25.201
to be called Flood Ranch,

00:00:25.201 --> 00:00:26.740
but they changed the name

00:00:26.740 --> 00:00:27.940
'cause there was a lot
of frogs right there

00:00:27.940 --> 00:00:29.250
by the river bottom,

00:00:29.250 --> 00:00:31.130
so they changed us to Canta Ranas,

00:00:31.130 --> 00:00:33.020
which in English means singing frogs

00:00:33.020 --> 00:00:35.200
and in my hood, you couldn't be

00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:37.443
from my neighborhood unless
you had family members.

00:00:37.443 --> 00:00:39.140
Maybe your brother, your sister,

00:00:39.140 --> 00:00:40.060
your daddy or mom.

00:00:40.060 --> 00:00:41.030
If you didn't have nobody,

00:00:41.030 --> 00:00:42.410
no kind of family members in the hood,

00:00:42.410 --> 00:00:43.587
you couldn't get in.

00:00:43.587 --> 00:00:47.050
And that lasted till about 89.

00:00:47.050 --> 00:00:50.100
After that, went a
little bit different way,

00:00:50.100 --> 00:00:52.429
different, somebody created an action

00:00:52.429 --> 00:00:55.810
and what he did was we got at him

00:00:55.810 --> 00:00:56.770
and we let him know he wanted to get

00:00:56.770 --> 00:00:58.620
in the hood so bad, but he couldn't get in

00:00:58.620 --> 00:00:59.960
'cause he didn't have no family members,

00:00:59.960 --> 00:01:01.980
so one of the guys threw out there okay,

00:01:01.980 --> 00:01:03.980
well, bring us two bodies
and you can get in.

00:01:03.980 --> 00:01:05.840
Well, he didn't bring two, he brought five

00:01:05.840 --> 00:01:07.104
in one weekend.

00:01:07.104 --> 00:01:09.725
So we let him him, so
he broke that tradition.

00:01:09.725 --> 00:01:11.469
That's my homie today.

00:01:11.469 --> 00:01:13.100
Right now he's in Pelican Bay.

00:01:13.100 --> 00:01:15.211
He's doing about 80 years.

00:01:15.211 --> 00:01:16.970
He broke the tradition,

00:01:16.970 --> 00:01:18.732
so that tradition was broken.

00:01:18.732 --> 00:01:20.927
Me, I didn't really agree with it

00:01:20.927 --> 00:01:23.500
due to that fact that I feel that

00:01:23.500 --> 00:01:24.747
if you know somebody for a long time

00:01:24.747 --> 00:01:26.820
since say grammar school,

00:01:26.820 --> 00:01:29.240
they're most likely not to tell on you,

00:01:29.240 --> 00:01:31.850
but nowadays you get people
from other cities and stuff.

00:01:31.850 --> 00:01:33.600
There's no type of,

00:01:33.600 --> 00:01:34.537
there's not type of-

00:01:34.537 --> 00:01:35.370
- [Mark] Loyalty.

00:01:35.370 --> 00:01:38.290
- Yeah, loyalty or comradery there.

00:01:38.290 --> 00:01:39.890
But I been from my neighborhood

00:01:39.890 --> 00:01:41.229
since the age of 13.

00:01:41.229 --> 00:01:42.698
I've had my teardrop.

00:01:42.698 --> 00:01:44.300
That was the first tattoo I got.

00:01:44.300 --> 00:01:45.279
I got it at 15 years old.

00:01:45.279 --> 00:01:47.150
- [Mark] What does the
teardrop tattoo signify?

00:01:47.150 --> 00:01:48.210
- Well, you know it didn't represent

00:01:48.210 --> 00:01:49.640
that I had been to prison for a few years,

00:01:49.640 --> 00:01:50.750
'cause I was only 15

00:01:50.750 --> 00:01:51.840
and I wanted it filled it in,

00:01:51.840 --> 00:01:55.440
so it really represents
when you do the deed.

00:01:55.440 --> 00:01:56.962
In other words, you take care of business.

00:01:56.962 --> 00:01:58.582
You put somebody in the dirt.

00:01:58.582 --> 00:02:01.008
So I earned my teardrop at 15 years old.

00:02:01.008 --> 00:02:01.841
- [Mark] 15.

00:02:01.841 --> 00:02:03.190
- And it's been on my face since then.

00:02:03.190 --> 00:02:05.290
I was gonna remove it,

00:02:05.290 --> 00:02:07.250
but my little girl,
she's from neighborhood,

00:02:07.250 --> 00:02:08.680
she's my home girl, she told me nah,

00:02:08.680 --> 00:02:11.400
that if I removed it, it wouldn't be me,

00:02:11.400 --> 00:02:13.450
so I left it on my face.

00:02:13.450 --> 00:02:15.810
I went to prison, did 17 years,

00:02:15.810 --> 00:02:18.710
but I've been to juvenile hall, YA.

00:02:18.710 --> 00:02:22.160
I've been to placement
juvenile camp three times

00:02:22.160 --> 00:02:24.450
and I went to prison first time

00:02:24.450 --> 00:02:26.465
for two counts of kidnap

00:02:26.465 --> 00:02:28.900
and I was picked up for
three counts of murder

00:02:28.900 --> 00:02:30.810
and four counts of kidnap.

00:02:30.810 --> 00:02:32.780
They ended up convicting
me of two counts of kidnap.

00:02:32.780 --> 00:02:34.750
They gave me 15 years.

00:02:34.750 --> 00:02:37.200
I did seven out of that,

00:02:37.200 --> 00:02:38.033
got out for a year.

00:02:38.033 --> 00:02:40.760
I went back and did seven more straight,

00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:43.430
got out and then went
back and did four more.

00:02:43.430 --> 00:02:45.360
Right now I just barely got off parole.

00:02:45.360 --> 00:02:46.590
So right now I'm doing all right.

00:02:46.590 --> 00:02:48.000
- [Mark] So you just got out?

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:48.833
- Yeah.

00:02:48.833 --> 00:02:51.040
I've been out for about two years now,

00:02:51.040 --> 00:02:53.257
but I been to the county
here and there, you know.

00:02:53.257 --> 00:02:56.160
But the longest I did
was seven years straight.

00:02:56.160 --> 00:02:58.043
They had gave me seven years or 80% for

00:02:58.043 --> 00:02:59.836
a 20 sack of crystal meth.

00:02:59.836 --> 00:03:01.426
They gave me seven years for that.

00:03:01.426 --> 00:03:02.259
- [Mark] Seven years for that?

00:03:02.259 --> 00:03:03.680
- Yeah, they were trying to strike me out,

00:03:03.680 --> 00:03:05.360
trying to give me 25 to life

00:03:05.360 --> 00:03:07.140
for a 20 bag of glass.

00:03:07.140 --> 00:03:08.250
I ended up having to take a deal

00:03:08.250 --> 00:03:10.333
for seven years of 80%.

00:03:10.333 --> 00:03:11.730
I did every seven.

00:03:11.730 --> 00:03:13.678
I did it over till the last day.

00:03:13.678 --> 00:03:15.285
I was in there getting high.

00:03:15.285 --> 00:03:17.310
I was in there stabbing people, you know.

00:03:17.310 --> 00:03:18.909
Went to the shoot program

00:03:18.909 --> 00:03:20.883
and then that's when I got affiliated.

00:03:21.786 --> 00:03:25.721
They took me, sent a packet to Sacramento

00:03:25.721 --> 00:03:29.006
to see if they could, in other words,

00:03:29.006 --> 00:03:31.560
place me with these gentlemen

00:03:31.560 --> 00:03:33.980
and I didn't have no
photos with anybody in it,

00:03:33.980 --> 00:03:35.578
I didn't have no letters.

00:03:35.578 --> 00:03:37.560
I didn't have no identifying marks.

00:03:37.560 --> 00:03:39.955
One thing about me is I
never got any type of marks

00:03:39.955 --> 00:03:43.720
except this one where it affiliated me,

00:03:43.720 --> 00:03:45.070
where they could see my body

00:03:45.070 --> 00:03:47.420
and say well, that tattoo
right there means something.

00:03:47.420 --> 00:03:49.100
All my tattoos meant something.

00:03:49.100 --> 00:03:50.857
I got my daughter's name, my wife's name

00:03:50.857 --> 00:03:51.780
and my frogs.

00:03:51.780 --> 00:03:53.720
- [Mark] You have a lot
of frogs on your back.

00:03:53.720 --> 00:03:55.440
- Yeah, I wanted to earn my frogs.

00:03:55.440 --> 00:03:57.330
I got seven total.

00:03:57.330 --> 00:03:58.650
In my hood you had to earn them.

00:03:58.650 --> 00:04:00.010
If you didn't earn them,

00:04:00.010 --> 00:04:01.678
then we would take you out ourselves.

00:04:01.678 --> 00:04:04.360
One of my little homie ended
up getting five frogs on him.

00:04:04.360 --> 00:04:05.193
He didn't earned them,

00:04:05.193 --> 00:04:07.334
so they killed him like a week later.

00:04:07.334 --> 00:04:10.133
- [Mark] These frogs represent what?

00:04:10.133 --> 00:04:11.825
- It represents a soul.

00:04:11.825 --> 00:04:12.660
- Somebody you-

00:04:12.660 --> 00:04:13.833
Somebody's soul.

00:04:13.833 --> 00:04:15.330
So once you get a soul,

00:04:15.330 --> 00:04:16.777
you can put it on your body.

00:04:16.777 --> 00:04:17.610
- [Mark] Understood.

00:04:17.610 --> 00:04:19.060
- Yeah, one of my homies didn't earn it,

00:04:19.060 --> 00:04:20.580
so they killed him.

00:04:20.580 --> 00:04:21.611
My other homie that earned,

00:04:21.611 --> 00:04:22.807
he had a triple murder,

00:04:22.807 --> 00:04:24.360
he put three frogs on him,

00:04:24.360 --> 00:04:26.210
this guy put five, so
they guy that had three

00:04:26.210 --> 00:04:28.860
killed the guy with five
'cause he never earned them.

00:04:28.860 --> 00:04:30.670
Mainly I was the one
that used to find people

00:04:30.670 --> 00:04:33.192
that couldn't get found.

00:04:33.192 --> 00:04:34.460
I used to go undercover.

00:04:34.460 --> 00:04:35.973
I've had my hair red.

00:04:37.450 --> 00:04:39.264
I've had my hair blonde.

00:04:39.264 --> 00:04:41.888
I've shaved my mustache off, wore glasses.

00:04:41.888 --> 00:04:43.891
I grew my hair long, shaved my head.

00:04:43.891 --> 00:04:46.600
I used to change my identity a lot.

00:04:46.600 --> 00:04:48.220
- [Mark] So change your identity.

00:04:48.220 --> 00:04:49.053
- Yes.

00:04:49.053 --> 00:04:50.420
- To protect yourself from?

00:04:50.420 --> 00:04:51.914
- Getting found, getting caught.

00:04:51.914 --> 00:04:52.870
- [Mark] By who?

00:04:52.870 --> 00:04:54.385
- By the FBI for a while.

00:04:54.385 --> 00:04:55.287
- [Mark] The FBI?

00:04:55.287 --> 00:04:57.420
- Yeah, the FBI was on me for a while.

00:04:57.420 --> 00:04:58.616
They were on me for maybe out,

00:04:58.616 --> 00:05:01.351
total they were on me for about 10 years

00:05:01.351 --> 00:05:04.160
due to the fact that I
had five family members

00:05:04.160 --> 00:05:05.487
that were those guys.

00:05:05.487 --> 00:05:08.130
- [Mark] You could pass for Caucasian

00:05:08.130 --> 00:05:08.963
with blonde hair.

00:05:08.963 --> 00:05:10.660
- Yeah, yeah, I could, exactly.

00:05:10.660 --> 00:05:12.128
I used to cover up my tattoos with makeup.

00:05:12.128 --> 00:05:13.173
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:05:13.173 --> 00:05:14.067
- I used to do a lot of things.

00:05:14.067 --> 00:05:16.352
Sometimes I had my
mustache trimmed real small

00:05:16.352 --> 00:05:18.670
or I let my goatee and mustache

00:05:18.670 --> 00:05:20.610
and I'll shave it real thin,

00:05:20.610 --> 00:05:21.443
you know what I mean?

00:05:21.443 --> 00:05:23.580
Sometimes I wore glasses.

00:05:23.580 --> 00:05:24.563
I've had red hair before.

00:05:24.563 --> 00:05:25.396
- [Mark] Red hair.

00:05:25.396 --> 00:05:26.860
- Yeah, I had red hair before.

00:05:26.860 --> 00:05:28.700
They were looking for me for,

00:05:28.700 --> 00:05:29.533
they were looking for me

00:05:29.533 --> 00:05:32.380
for a double murder and
I changed my hair to red,

00:05:32.380 --> 00:05:33.860
but they ended up busting my homie.

00:05:33.860 --> 00:05:36.360
It's just that me and him
had the same first name.

00:05:37.940 --> 00:05:39.956
- [Mark] So in prison, which you've spent

00:05:39.956 --> 00:05:40.981
half you life in, right?

00:05:40.981 --> 00:05:42.120
- Yes.

00:05:42.120 --> 00:05:42.989
- [Mark] In prison.

00:05:42.989 --> 00:05:46.913
How different is the
gang world than outside

00:05:46.913 --> 00:05:48.640
- What's the different in the gang world?

00:05:48.640 --> 00:05:50.772
Out here, there's more room to get around.

00:05:50.772 --> 00:05:52.040
There's more things you can do

00:05:52.040 --> 00:05:53.510
and get away with 'cause you can duck

00:05:53.510 --> 00:05:54.730
and hide and maneuver.

00:05:54.730 --> 00:05:56.471
In prison, you ain't going nowhere.

00:05:56.471 --> 00:05:57.553
You can't hide, you can't duck.

00:05:57.553 --> 00:06:00.094
You know, you gotta
face everything head on.

00:06:00.094 --> 00:06:01.610
The way I learned it best

00:06:01.610 --> 00:06:03.830
is if you did it, you did it.

00:06:03.830 --> 00:06:04.727
There's one thing I did,

00:06:04.727 --> 00:06:06.450
they asked me stab somebody,

00:06:06.450 --> 00:06:07.415
I end up stabbing them

00:06:07.415 --> 00:06:08.660
and then the other guy asked me

00:06:08.660 --> 00:06:09.887
why'd you stab him?

00:06:09.887 --> 00:06:12.286
I said, well, I felt it
was the right thing to do.

00:06:12.286 --> 00:06:14.300
I was the type of person
if I did something wrong,

00:06:14.300 --> 00:06:15.206
well, then stab me.

00:06:15.206 --> 00:06:17.421
And due to the fact that I carried myself

00:06:17.421 --> 00:06:22.060
at a certain level, well
my punishment was severe.

00:06:22.060 --> 00:06:24.570
My punishment wasn't do 50 pushups

00:06:24.570 --> 00:06:26.085
or do 113 burpees.

00:06:26.085 --> 00:06:29.840
My punishment was they would get a knife

00:06:29.840 --> 00:06:31.205
and maybe they would make the handle,

00:06:31.205 --> 00:06:33.610
they'd make the handle
about five inches long

00:06:33.610 --> 00:06:34.950
and you got the seven-inch knife,

00:06:34.950 --> 00:06:37.470
so they would leave about
may an inch and a half out

00:06:37.470 --> 00:06:38.660
and they would stab you with that.

00:06:38.660 --> 00:06:40.431
And that's just a checking.

00:06:40.431 --> 00:06:43.076
More or less that's just
don't do that again.

00:06:43.076 --> 00:06:44.630
I wouldn't get beat down,

00:06:44.630 --> 00:06:45.527
I wouldn't get regulated.

00:06:45.527 --> 00:06:47.150
Yeah, because I knew better.

00:06:47.150 --> 00:06:48.550
I had been to prison.

00:06:48.550 --> 00:06:50.610
There was no excuse for this black dude

00:06:50.610 --> 00:06:52.300
bought an ice cream and I went

00:06:52.300 --> 00:06:53.900
and got his ice cream and took a bite.

00:06:53.900 --> 00:06:54.914
I know better than that.

00:06:54.914 --> 00:06:56.770
But if I did take a bite, well, then

00:06:56.770 --> 00:06:58.809
my punishment would be severely.

00:06:58.809 --> 00:07:00.452
You know I've been stabbed twice

00:07:00.452 --> 00:07:02.630
just getting checked,
you know what I mean?

00:07:02.630 --> 00:07:05.210
And each time I got
stabbed about seven times.

00:07:05.210 --> 00:07:07.904
But it was just because
I needed to get checked

00:07:07.904 --> 00:07:10.087
in a level I carried myself on.

00:07:10.087 --> 00:07:12.321
You know, I already been
to prison five times.

00:07:12.321 --> 00:07:14.440
There was no excuse for me more or less

00:07:14.440 --> 00:07:15.620
and I'm a strong believer in that.

00:07:15.620 --> 00:07:17.531
I'm a strong believer in you get punished

00:07:17.531 --> 00:07:22.531
in the, we'll say at this level

00:07:23.673 --> 00:07:25.745
because you carry yourself at this level.

00:07:25.745 --> 00:07:27.365
A lot of things can be told

00:07:27.365 --> 00:07:29.110
but in a certain way.

00:07:29.110 --> 00:07:30.510
You know there's
information I can give you,

00:07:30.510 --> 00:07:31.640
but there's certain information,

00:07:31.640 --> 00:07:33.245
vital information that I can't give you.

00:07:33.245 --> 00:07:36.770
As in names, places, but I
can speak of things I did

00:07:38.029 --> 00:07:39.730
in my life, you know what I mean

00:07:39.730 --> 00:07:40.849
and I did it all.

00:07:40.849 --> 00:07:43.839
I've heard about things
that dudes did in prison,

00:07:43.839 --> 00:07:47.050
like I heard about a guy
that they sent four dudes

00:07:47.050 --> 00:07:49.390
to stab this guy and he stabbed them all.

00:07:49.390 --> 00:07:50.530
Well, when that came about to me

00:07:50.530 --> 00:07:53.060
and they sent four dudes at
me, I did the same thing.

00:07:53.060 --> 00:07:54.007
I stabbed all four of them

00:07:54.007 --> 00:07:55.047
and they were supposed to come and get me

00:07:55.047 --> 00:07:56.720
and I ended up stabbing all of them.

00:07:56.720 --> 00:07:58.210
So apparently they sent the wrong guys

00:07:58.210 --> 00:07:59.920
to get at me, so what they did is

00:07:59.920 --> 00:08:01.700
they didn't try it again,
you know what I mean?

00:08:01.700 --> 00:08:03.355
And that was simply out of hate,

00:08:03.355 --> 00:08:05.531
out of people just not liking me,

00:08:05.531 --> 00:08:07.685
not liking the way I did things.

00:08:07.685 --> 00:08:10.420
Like I was saying, I was
19 years old in prison

00:08:10.420 --> 00:08:11.610
and I was running all the Centinela

00:08:11.610 --> 00:08:13.769
and that was level four and level three

00:08:13.769 --> 00:08:15.287
and I was only 19 years old.

00:08:15.287 --> 00:08:16.608
You known what I mean?

00:08:16.608 --> 00:08:17.490
I was speaking to gentlemen

00:08:17.490 --> 00:08:19.280
that were 45, 50,

00:08:19.280 --> 00:08:20.979
been to prison like 10, 15 years

00:08:20.979 --> 00:08:22.877
and I had more rank than them

00:08:22.877 --> 00:08:24.650
for the simple fact was the way

00:08:24.650 --> 00:08:25.550
I carried myself.

00:08:25.550 --> 00:08:27.376
- [Mark] A lot of that has to do

00:08:27.376 --> 00:08:30.970
with the respect that you command.

00:08:30.970 --> 00:08:32.230
- And you earn, you know what I mean?

00:08:32.230 --> 00:08:33.820
Yeah, and I went to the county jail

00:08:33.820 --> 00:08:35.486
and the first time I
went through, you know,

00:08:35.486 --> 00:08:37.820
I didn't really do anything in general.

00:08:37.820 --> 00:08:38.950
I did my time and got out.

00:08:38.950 --> 00:08:39.970
The second time I went through,

00:08:39.970 --> 00:08:41.380
I went balls out.

00:08:41.380 --> 00:08:42.509
I stabbed everybody and anything,

00:08:42.509 --> 00:08:43.760
you know what I mean?

00:08:43.760 --> 00:08:46.890
I've ran five prisons, the whole prison,

00:08:46.890 --> 00:08:48.150
every yard, every dude.

00:08:48.150 --> 00:08:49.180
I was in charge of everybody.

00:08:49.180 --> 00:08:52.290
I ran Centinela, Ironwood,
Chuckwalla, Tehachapi

00:08:53.520 --> 00:08:55.997
and Delano and I'm talking about all five.

00:08:55.997 --> 00:08:57.470
Every dude on there,

00:08:57.470 --> 00:08:59.057
I was responsible for all of them.

00:08:59.057 --> 00:09:01.373
And I was 23 years old, 24 years old

